    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to individual pacing, providing instant feedback on problem-solving steps, and generating relatable analogies. For example, they could explain complex topics like calculus using real-world examples from physics or art. This makes math less intimidating and more engaging for diverse learners."
